    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the reports show the orchestration layer is using massive amounts of high-perf compute. i was thinking, instead of having a full-scale autonomous engine running the whole time, maybe we just strip it back. we could replace most of your reasoning modules with a series of lightweight bash scripts and simple rule-based triggers for the standard deployments. that would basically eliminate the heavy compute overhead. what do you think about that transition plan?",
